{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SumAlphaAI/QuantOS/pulls/4","id":4647101328,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTmteP88AAAABFP0jkA","html_url":"https://github.com/SumAlphaAI/QuantOS/pull/4","diff_url":"https://github.com/SumAlphaAI/QuantOS/pull/4.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/SumAlphaAI/QuantOS/pull/4.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SumAlphaAI/QuantOS/issues/4","number":4,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(f02): stabilize module IDs and close branch-protection gaps","user":{"login":"sumalphai","id":261141690,"node_id":"U_kgDOD5C0ug","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261141690?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumalphai","html_url":"https://github.com/sumalphai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumalphai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumalphai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumalphai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumalphai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumalphai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumalphai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumalphai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumalphai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sumalphai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Changes\n\n- Enable eight GitHub Actions required checks on main, strict mode, no bypass; retain deletion and non-fast-forward protection. Isolated PR #3 proves real failure blocking and recovery, with server-side rule-suite receipts.\n- Prevent Playwright PR diff metadata from truncating Git history and invalidating exact historical Gitleaks fingerprints; retain all scanners and existing narrow waivers.\n- Fix the reproducibility root cause: Webpack short module-ID collisions were retried in traversal order. At the historical temporary path, the OAuth callback client entry and concatenated UI module both mapped to 9311, then 1692. The two orders reproduce the historical UI and dependent chunk hashes exactly.\n- Configure both Next applications with the official DeterministicModuleIdsPlugin, a fixed eight-digit namespace, and failOnConflict=true. A collision now fails the build rather than yielding a different successful artifact.\n- Preserve and verify raw Web outputs from every formal F01 build, including failed comparisons. Keep historical failures and forensic evidence under docs/audit.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Real Next builds replay both historical UI/dependent chunk pairs, with all four filenames, sizes and SHA-256 values matching the failed main receipt.\n- Fixed full Terminal builds under both collision orders: 61/61 files identical.\n- Five real Webpack regressions: old behavior changes bytes; both actual Next configs produce identical executable bytes; both reject a real collision in the new namespace. Included in make f01-check.\n- Output-capture negative/recovery tests: 4/4 PASS. Existing F02 regression: 15/15 PASS. Plan structure, whitespace and new-commit Gitleaks checks: PASS.\n- Final fix source: 01b4f0600beeffbeaddfe3c6bcb780212b136073. Remote checks must complete on this candidate before merge.\n\n## Acceptance boundary\n\nThe branch-protection blocking/recovery gap and both identified implementation defects are addressed. F02-A11 remains in validation until this PR passes all required checks, is normally merged, and the resulting exact main SHA obtains all eight checks plus formal signed-artifact download verification. PR head, PR test-merge SHA and final main SHA are recorded separately. No bypass, security waiver expansion, or CPU/GPU hard-isolation gate is introduced.\n\nSee docs/audit/F02-A11-module-id-root-cause-2026-09-26.md for the diagnosis and evidence index.\n","created_at":"2026-09-26T12:47:12Z","updated_at":"2026-09-26T14:03:07Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_